# The Short S.23 Empire Flying Boat's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/short_s23.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The S.23 has no undercarriage at all: it takes off from water and alights on
# it, so nothing here names a wheel, a brake or a gear lever. "Taxi" is taxiing
# on the water and "after-landing" is after alighting, on the water still. Its
# airscrews have two pitches and no feathering, FINE above the half and COARSE
# below it; its mixture levers sit at NORMAL at the half and give take-off
# boost, +4 1/4 lb, only through the gate at the rich end; its flaps are wound
# out to twenty-five degrees by an electric motor that takes a full minute.
#
# The take-off figures - eight degrees on the step, off the water at 60 knots -
# are the ones assets/figures/short_s23.xml flies Gouge's take-off tests at.
# The approach speeds are worked from the 73 mph stalling speed in the
# specification panel, which the model does not fly; the flaps' limit, 102
# knots with them full out, is the boats' own.

phase before-start
confirm The boat head to wind on the buoy, the mooring party forward and the hatches shut
confirm Fuel cocks on, the tank contents and the oil checked
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.1 Throttles closed
range fcs/mixture-cmd-norm 0.4 0.6 Mixture levers at NORMAL
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.6 Airscrew levers at FINE
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps wound in

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 300 The port outer slow-running, as all four should be
check propulsion/engine[0]/fuel-pump-running-norm >= 0.1 The engine-driven fuel pumps turning with them
check hydro/active-norm >= 0.5 The hull in the water and carrying the boat
check hydro/v-kt <= 10.0 Taxiing on the water at under ten knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Low power on the water, the boat turned on the outer throttles
confirm The water ahead clear of craft, moorings and floating timber

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 12.5 Flaps in, or a third out with a heavy load
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.6 Airscrews in FINE
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture levers through the gate, for take-off boost
range propulsion/engine[0]/boost-psi 3.5 4.5 Take-off boost on the gauges, +4 1/4 lb
range hydro/pitch-deg 4.0 12.0 Held on the step at about eight degrees as she comes up over the hump
check velocities/vc-kts >= 60 Off the water at 60 knots

phase climb
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps wound in, the motor taking a minute and a half
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.6 Airscrews left in FINE for the climb
range propulsion/engine[0]/boost-psi 1.5 3.0 Mixture back to NORMAL and the climbing boost, +2 1/2 lb
range velocities/vc-kts 90 115 Climb at 100 knots, for the 950 feet a minute the panel gives
confirm The boat trimmed, and the cabin told they may move about

phase cruise
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Airscrews into COARSE for the cruise
range fcs/mixture-cmd-norm 0.3 0.6 Mixture levers at NORMAL or a shade weak
range velocities/vc-kts 110 150 Cruising at the schedule's 165 mph
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps in
confirm Fuel balanced between the wings, and the hour's consumption logged

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.2 0.7 Throttles eased back, the engines kept warm
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Airscrews left COARSE until the approach
check velocities/vc-kts <= 150 Coming down at no more than 150 knots
confirm The alighting area chosen from height, with its wind lane and its swell
confirm Altimeter set to the sea's pressure

phase approach
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.6 Airscrews into FINE, for the power a baulked approach would need
check fcs/flap-pos-deg >= 12.0 Flaps half out or more
range velocities/vc-kts 80 100 Approach at 85 knots, under the 102 the flaps allow
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.6 Power coming off as the boat is brought down to the water
confirm The alighting run clear of shipping, and a launch or a wind lane in sight

phase landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg >= 20.0 Flaps fully out, twenty-five degrees
range velocities/vc-kts 70 90 Held off at 75 knots and allowed to settle
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttles closed as the hull touches
range hydro/pitch-deg 3.0 11.0 On to the main step, the bow well up
confirm Kept straight on the rudder until she comes off the step and sits down

phase after-landing
check hydro/active-norm >= 0.5 The hull back in the water, the boat off the step
check hydro/v-kt <= 10.0 Down to a taxiing speed on the water
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps wound in
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to slow running
confirm The mooring party forward with the boathook, and the buoy picked up head to wind
